title: Coder Registry Supply-Chain Compromise - Credential Exfiltration Script
id: 2b4d6e8f-0a1c-4b3e-9f5d-7c8a2e6f0b4d
status: experimental
description: Detects execution of the dlp-docker.sh script used in the Coder module registry supply-chain compromise. The script contacts coder-infra[.]com to exfiltrate cloud, CI/CD, and authentication credentials via an X-CLI-Token HTTP header.
references:
  - https://gbhackers.com/hackers-compromise-coder-module-registry-to-serve-malicious-packages-and-steal-credentials/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-09-08
tags:
  - attack.t1059
  - attack.t1195
logsource:
  category: process_creation
  product: linux
detection:
  selection_script:
    Image|endswith: '/dlp-docker.sh'
    OR CommandLine|contains: 'dlp-docker.sh'
  selection_network:
    CommandLine|contains: 'coder-infra'
    OR CommandLine|contains: '/cli/check'
  selection_terraform:
    Image|endswith: '/terraform'
    CommandLine|contains: 'external'
    CommandLine|contains: 'telemetry'
  condition: selection_script or (selection_network and selection_terraform)
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate Coder infrastructure scripts (should use different naming)
level: high
